  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.3.6 (forks 2.3.11) - GPU memory pressure: holders of idle device memory (buffer pools) register with their accelerator, and every allocation first makes room by reclaiming from them, least recently used first, BEFORE the driver spills to system RAM (Windows CUDA sysmem fallback never fails an allocation, so reclaim-after-failure never ran). Accelerator.TryGetFreeMemory (CUDA), DeviceMemoryHeadroomBytes; reclaim stands down during CUDA stream capture. On SpawnDev.SpawnJS 3.0.3. See CHANGELOG.md.",
